# Rust / Tauri command rules

Before adding or changing commands, read `docs/command-registry.md` and `docs/core-boundaries.md`.

## Module map

- Stable: `commands/core.rs`, `organizer.rs`, `auth.rs`, `account.rs`, `diagnostics.rs`, …
- Experimental: `commands/experimental.rs` + `#[cfg(feature = "experimental")]` only
- `commands.rs` stays a thin registry/re-export — do not dump logic there

## Checklist for each new command

1. Assign module + risk class
2. Document input scope and mutation behavior
3. Require approval for `local-mutate` / `os-control` / `external-mutate` as appropriate
4. Register in `lib.rs` `generate_handler!` without reordering unrelated entries
5. Add tests for valid / invalid / denied / interrupted paths where practical
6. Update `docs/command-registry.md` in the same PR

## Trust invariants in code

- Organizer: never delete; never overwrite; undo journal before mutate
- `organizer_execute` re-plans server-side — do not accept a plan from the frontend
- Policy engine (`policy/`) stays pure (no IO)
- Experimental AI/cloud/vision/knowledge stay feature-gated
